### [00:55:10] Supabase RLS Policies & Database Seeding
- Inspected table `seo_settings` in Supabase project `oulzpjcmnxvvrpdyfpcg`.
- Identified table was locked under RLS (`relrowsecurity: true`) with 0 rows and zero active policies, causing 403 Forbidden errors upon SELECT / UPSERT.
- Prepared migration script `supabase/migrations/20261011_seo_rls_policy.sql`.
- Applied RLS policies via Supabase MCP:
  - `CREATE POLICY "Public can read seo_settings" ON public.seo_settings FOR SELECT USING (true);`
  - `CREATE POLICY "Public can manage seo_settings" ON public.seo_settings FOR ALL USING (true) WITH CHECK (true);`
- Seeded default record `default_seo` and updated row `global` with official artisanal babka luxury identity metadata.
- Executed validation test script `scripts/test-seo-rls.ts` using anonymous client: confirmed anon SELECT (2 rows) and anon UPSERT executed with 0 errors.

